# The pins that MORE THAN ONE consumer needs.
#
# Format is KEY=value with no spaces around the `=`, for one reason: Make reads
# it with `include` and bash reads it with `.` — natively, both of them, with no
# parser in between. That is the whole design.
#
# It sits beside install-dev-tools.sh so ONE path expression resolves in both
# places it is read from: `$(dirname "$0")/versions.env` works in a checkout
# (toolbelt/) and in the image (/tmp/, where the Dockerfiles COPY the pair).
# Same trick as lib/ckcommon.sh — no image-vs-checkout branch to keep in sync.
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE: a pin with two or more readers. PHPUNIT has two — the
# Makefile runs the tool test suites on the same phar this image bakes, which is
# what the old "same phar and same hash as install-dev-tools.sh; bump both
# together" comment in lint.yml was asking a human to remember.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT: a pin with one reader. Every other version in
# install-dev-tools.sh (phpstan, rector, psalm, civix, mago, npm, infection,
# coder) is used there and nowhere else, and moving it here would only put the
# value further from the comment that explains it. Same for actionlint and
# zizmor, whose only consumer is the Makefile, and CK_TRIVY_* in
# build-dev-images.yml. A file that collects pins it does not need to share is
# just a second place to look.
#
# The CK_ prefix keeps these clear of the same-named build ARGs, so a
# `--build-arg PHPUNIT_VERSION=…` still wins over the default it feeds.

# PHPUnit 9 is the last line CiviCRM's test base supports; the patch is pinned
# too. Re-derive the hash after a bump with `curl -LsS <url> | sha256sum`.
CK_PHPUNIT_VERSION=9.6.35
CK_PHPUNIT_SHA256=f39d634a5e5bcafd71565b33328ae4fb173703296c12ac94a24550cb8291e964
